{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall keep apart.</b> נְזִירָה is nothing but separation, and so it says ״וַיִּנָּזֵר מֵאַחֲרַי״ (Ezekiel 14), ״נָזֹרוּ אָחוֹר״ (Isaiah 1) — let them separate from the sacred donations during their days of impurity (Sifra)." "<b>And they shall keep apart from the sacred donations of the children of Israel, which they sanctify to Me, and they shall not profane My holy name.</b> Rearrange the verse and expound it." "<b>Which they sanctify to Me.</b> To include the sacred donations of the priests themselves."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:38.008829632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}